SNESEmulator
Copyright 2026 Nils Kopal

SharpPixels, bitmap menu font, PCM output and TLS/relay transport are derived
from Nils Kopal's C64Emulator (Apache-2.0), local source snapshot:
f01750e17a2c3f4cabfd57dc0c470dac93a91a23
https://github.com/n1k0m0/C64Emulator

The SNES hardware core, cartridge loader, frontend integration, diagnostic ROM
generator and tests were developed for this project. No C64 hardware core,
commercial game ROM, Nintendo firmware or third-party SNES core is included.

OpenTK and NAudio are restored as NuGet dependencies under their respective
licenses. See the package metadata for third-party license information.

SingleStepTests SPC700 test vectors are MIT-licensed, Copyright2024
SingleStepTests. The redistributed offline samples retain their license at
testdata/spc700-sample/LICENSE. Full vectors are local test inputs, not shipped
with the emulator. No external SPC700 implementation source was incorporated.

The external VRAM mid-scanline test ROM and retained source are Copyright
2022 Marcus Rowe (undisbeliever), Zlib license. See
testdata/ppu-external/upstream-LICENSE and testdata/m5-ppu-manifest.json.
It is laboratory test data; no third-party emulator core code is included.

Manager library metadata uses Microsoft.Data.Sqlite10.0.10 (Microsoft, MIT),
SQLitePCLRaw.bundle_e_sqlite3/config/core/provider3.0.5 (SourceGear, Apache-2.0),
and its SQLite3.53.4 native dependency (SQLite public domain). Exact dependency
versions are retained in NuGet lockfiles; no UI framework beyond built-in WPF.
The C64 Manager concept informed the architecture; its untracked files were read
only and have not been incorporated or modified.

DSP1 research uses the NEC1989 manufacturer databook and Nintendo developer
manual, with source/scan identities documented in docs/m10a-dsp1.md. The own C#
uPD7725 is independent of the laboratory-only bsnes reference (byuu et al,
GPL-3.0-or-later); no reference core or firmware bytes are distributed. The
public numerical reference traces are separate from original hardware evidence.
Board/interface documentation is credited to Overload and the Snes9x DSP Team;
the original firmware dump identity source is credited to Caitsith2/byuu.
